  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="transcription" xml:id="transcription_aad_0185" xml:lang="en">
          <div type="letter">
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00556/" ed="1r" type="sheet"/>
            <div type="letter_message" hand="#type_black_luke">
              <opener>
                <seg>
                  <lb/><space quantity="45" unit="char"/>as from
                </seg>
                <seg hand="#print_luke">
                  <lb/><hi rend="italic" hand="#print_luke">From <persName><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_89">Dr. F. D. Luke</rs></persName>, <orgName><rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_6">Christ Church</rs></orgName>, <placeName><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_46">Oxford</rs></placeName></hi>. <seg hand="#type_black_luke">(<foreign xml:lang="de">z.Zt.</foreign><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_808">Shotheids</rs>)</seg> <hi rend="italic" hand="#print_luke">Tel. Oxford 41357</hi>
                </seg>
                <dateline hand="#hand_black_luke">
                  <date>
                    <lb/>4 Sept. 73
                  </date>
                </dateline>
                <salute hand="#hand_black_luke">
                  <lb/>Dear <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">Wystan</rs>
                </salute>
              </opener>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="5" unit="char"/>It's <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">d</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">s</add></subst>ad about <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_41">Tolkien</rs>. I'm very sorry you didn't see him again. As for
                <lb/>myself, one of the things I shall most regret all my life is missing an eve<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">h</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">n</add></subst>ing
                <lb/>on which, soon after he came back to <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_46">Oxford</rs>, <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_830">Eric Dodd<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">'</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">s</add></subst></rs> brought him into dinner
                <lb/>and afterwards in CR, I'm told, he talked for ages about his work - I didn't
                <lb/>stay for CR because, absurdly, I failed to real<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">l</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">i</add></subst>se who Eric's guest was.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="3" unit="char"/>I've now done the remaining <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_564"><hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_luke">Ro<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">a</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">m</add></subst>an Elegies</hi></rs> and revised the others as best I
                <lb/>can and added the inevitable annotations (that was a labour, but interesting)
                <lb/>- I think the latter should all come together at th<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke"><gap reason="illegible" quantity="1" unit="char"></gap></del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">e</add></subst> end.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>This Xerox copy isn't
                <lb/>very clear, I'm afraid, but the best I can do in these parts, short of retyping
                <lb/>the lot - this will have to be done in the end of course before the thing is
                <lb/>sent to <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_831">Peter Jay</rs>, but I didn't want to ask the Tutors' Secretar<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">t</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">y</add></subst> to begin that
                <lb/>until hearing from you whether you have any suggestions about further alterations.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="3" unit="char"/>I thought again about the problem of the metre and tried to clarify <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">n6</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">my</add></subst> ideas
                <lb/>(see Notes)<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">:</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">;</add></subst> they seem more or less to agree with the principles underlying yo<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">r</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">u</add></subst>r
                <lb/><rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_566">"Natural Linguistics"</rs> and your piece in hexameters about insects (what a <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_luke"><subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">a</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">d</add></subst>amne</hi>d
                <lb/>good poem that is! I didn't re<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">l</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">a</add></subst>lly take it in till the other day; and how I
                <lb/>agree with what it says - <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_luke">pace</hi> St.Isaac the Syrian, apud Lossky "The Mystical
                <lb/>Theology of the <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke"><unclear>O</unclear></del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">E</add></subst>astern Ch." which I am currently reading with great admiration;
                <lb/>he wrote that one should be "burning with charity for the whole of creation,
                <lb/>for men, for the birds, for the beasts, for the demons"(!)"-for all cr<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">w</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">e</add></subst>atures...
                <lb/>Such a man never ceases to pray also for the animals, for the enemies of Truth,
                <lb/>and for those who do him ev<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">ei</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">il</add></subst>, that they may be preserved an purified. He will
                <lb/>pray even for the reptiles, moved by the infinite pity <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">e</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">w</add></subst>hich" etc.etc. Rather
                <lb/>a tall order).
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="3" unit="char"/>I hope you &amp; Chester are well.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I heard you were on great form at the Poetry
                <lb/>International and were very kind to my friend Al<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">si</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">is</add></subst>on Weir who was somehow
                <lb/>smuggled into your pr<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">r</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">e</add></subst>sence. I'm not going abroad this vac, but just spending
                <lb/>2 or 3 weeks up here in Scotland.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>When I am in Oxford and think about Shot-
                <lb/>heids I feel it is madness not <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">s</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">t</add></subst>o sell it or at least let it, but when I come
                <lb/>here the spell works again; especi<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">z</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">a</add></subst>lly this time, when the weather ha<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">d</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">s</add></subst> been
                <lb/>elvishl<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke"><unclear>Z</unclear></del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">y</add></subst> beautiful, and even Beelzebub's creatures have for some reason been
                <lb/>troubling me less this season (though there is a curious recrudescence ofthings
                <lb/>- ?birds - going bump agianst the win<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">o</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">d</add></subst>ow in the early morning).
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="3" unit="char"/>I had a bad depression all <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">m</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">M</add></subst>ay and June, for a comp<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">e</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">l</add></subst>exity of reasons which
                <lb/>weren't <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">v</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">c</add></subst>lear, though <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">i</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">I</add></subst> suppose Matty was an important one. However that seems 
                <lb/>to have settled into the usual "as good as can be reasonably expected" (and at
                <lb/>any rate <hi rend="underline" hand="#hand_black_luke">much</hi> better than the situation with his German predecessor). Our
                <lb/>meetings <foreign xml:lang="de">un<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">r</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">t</add></subst>er vier Augen</foreign> are rare, but the <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke"><unclear>ß</unclear></del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">l</add></subst>ast two at least were very good,
                <lb/>with a lot of mutual communication, and made up for a great deal (in July"Figaro"
                <lb/>at Glyn<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">e</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">d</add></subst>ebourne, to which I did NOT ask his girl-friend; and in August a tuto<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">a</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">r</add></subst>rial
                <lb/>- sic - on Goethe's poetry, sitting out in the garden after lunch at an inn away
                <lb/>up the Thames valley).<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>Hedoes seem (hard as I <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">d</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">f</add></subst>ind it to believe the evidence)
                <lb/>to be fond of me and admire me, but demands an incredible amount of "stimulation"
                <lb/>and "encouragement" (he equates the two, which seems strange to me) and when he
                <lb/>doesn't get it I am in no uncertain terms called cynical, insensitive, unintui-
                <lb/>tive, etc. At least I am being obliged to rethink my ways as a tutor. I hope
                <lb/>to see something of h<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">k</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">i</add></subst>m in Edinburgh this week. Later in the month he <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">h</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">g</add></subst>oes off
              </p>
            </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00557/" ed="1v" type="sheet"/>
            <div type="letter_message" hand="#type_black_luke">
              <p>
                <lb/>for his year in Paris. I plan to take the Hilary Term off on sabbatical (to
                <lb/>try and get on with that bloody Kleist project) and shall go abroad for a
                <lb/>b<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">j</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">i</add></subst>t then, not without passing at least <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">w</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">o</add></subst>nce through <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">p</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">P</add></subst>aris.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="3" unit="char"/>A major row has been blowing up between the Ch.Ch<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">,</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">.</add></subst> undergraduates and the
                <lb/>Ch.Ch. <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">e</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">E</add></subst>stablishment about the question of women guests overnight in college.
                <lb/>Many of <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">t</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">u</add></subst>s think it could have been better handled. A special pre-Term GB
                <lb/>meeting has even been called, "to receive a statement from the Senior Censor
                <lb/>concerning a disciplinary matter..."; this in i<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">n</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">t</add></subst>self makes history, never
                <lb/>having happened before. Militancy has begun and more is promised; no doubt you
                <lb/>will be there to see &amp; hear part of the fun.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>In general next term is going to
                <lb/>be hell for me, with much too much teaching to do (the price of absence in
                <lb/><subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">N</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">H</add></subst>ilary).<space quantity="3" unit="char"/>I look forward to hearing from you on the <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_luke">Elegies</hi>. It would be
                <lb/>nice if we could manage to get our <del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke"><unclear>beit</unclear></del> bit done <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">n</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">b</add></subst>efore term begins (delivery
                <lb/>da<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">y</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">t</add></subst>e is December.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>Incidentally there has been complete and unexplained silence
                <lb/>on the Chicago side b<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">e</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">o</add></subst>th from their man and from my agent). <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke"><subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">§</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">a</add></subst></del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">A</add></subst>s to the historical
                <lb/>/factual details which you may require for your pref<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">ea</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">ac</add></subst>e, all I can send you
                <lb/>from up here is a f<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke"><unclear>r</unclear></del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">e</add></subst>w relevant lines from Staiger's edition, but I'll have a
                <lb/>look at the others when I get back <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">f</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">t</add></subst>o Oxford.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="3" unit="char"/>I'm sorry there was that muddle about the forwarding of your ma<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">k</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">i</add></subst>l - the
                <lb/>Steward's employees are almost all imbeciles.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="3" unit="char"/>Incidentally I continue to get on well with Matty's mother (spent a weekend
                <lb/>at the family mansion at the end of July) - she is very beautiful, charm<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">k</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">i</add></subst>ng
                <lb/>and amusing, and I'm having her to dinner at High Table on Sat.Nov.l0th, when
                <lb/>I hope you will be there (I gave her "<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">G</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">F</add></subst>orewords and Afterw<unclear><subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">a</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">o</add></subst></unclear>rds" for her birth-
                <lb/>day).
              </p>
              <closer hand="#hand_black_luke">
                <salute>
                  <lb/><unclear>l</unclear>ove
                </salute>
                <signed>
                  <lb/>David
                </signed>
              </closer>
            </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00558/" ed="2r" type="sheet"/>
            <div type="letter_message" hand="#type_black_luke">
              <p>
                <lb/>P.S.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I woke up early the other morning and this more or less came into my mind
                <lb/>(though tidied up slightly since). I can't possibly judge it. Should I (a) burn
                <lb/>it, (b) con<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">d</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">s</add></subst>ign it to some private file, (c) resume attempts at verse composition
                <lb/>of my own, as <subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_luke">s</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">w</add></subst>ell as translation?
              </p>
              <closer hand="#hand_black_luke">
                <salute>
                  <lb/><unclear>l</unclear>.
                </salute>
                <signed>
                  <lb/>D.
                </signed>
              </closer>
            </div>
            <div type="poem" hand="#type_cc_luke">
              <lg>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>Solution of mysteries, communication</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>broken and restor<del rend="overstrike" hand="#hand_black_luke"><gap reason="illegible" unit="char" quantity="1"></gap></del>ed, the missing syllables</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>floating now into place: you, you, you, you.</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>And swans drift past, one green and golden feathered,</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>more royal, following.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>Water and grass,</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>great trees, the orchard, fruit in netted beds</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>and against sunsoaked walls, g<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_cc_luke">r</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">l</add></subst>ass drawing sun</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>where flowers speak from half the world away.</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/><foreign xml:lang="de">Wo war ich s<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_cc_luke">h</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">c</add></subst>hon einmal und war so selig?</foreign></l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>A terrace where a flock of do<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_cc_luke">c</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">v</add></subst>es have <subst><del rend="overlaid" hand="#hand_black_luke">clustered</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#hand_black_luke">landed</add></subst></l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/><subst><del rend="overlaid" hand="#hand_black_luke">in patterns on the ground: read this,</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#hand_black_luke">clustered in patterns: I am to read</add></subst> their message.</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>Or if I cross th<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_cc_luke">t</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_luke">a</add></subst>t water, running, gliding,</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>there I shall find him, the shy forest-creature</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>who died and lives, and he will recognise me.</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>Who were you, are you, what are you telling me?</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>Tell me in time - if you can speak in time</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>and place, oh unpossessable, imperfect</l>
                <l><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>likeness, free, unforeseen, lost, lost, returning.</l>
              </lg>
              <ab>
                <lb/><space quantity="49" unit="char"/>27.8.73.
              </ab>
             </div>
              <div>
                <ab hand="#hand_blue_unident_0185">
                  <lb/>65
                </ab>
              </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00559/" ed="2v" type="sheet"/>
      </div>
     </div>
